<title>ITALY: Eridania opens US soya processing unit.</title>
<headline>Eridania opens US soya processing unit.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Soya, a U.S. unit of Eridania Beghin-Say, has opened a soya processing plant in Morristown, Indiana, its Italian parent company Montedison said in a statement.</p>
<p>The factory, in which $40 million has been invested, starts production in the next few weeks and will have initial crushing capacity of 2,000 tonnes per day.</p>
<p>Work to double capacity and create another refinery unit for soya oil will start later down the line, it said.</p>
</text>
